---
description: Security baseline for application, APIs, and infrastructure
alwaysApply: true
---

# Security Baseline

- Follow OWASP Top 10 controls and secure-by-default patterns.
- Never hardcode secrets, keys, tokens, or credentials.
- Validate and sanitize all external inputs.
- Apply least privilege to service accounts and IAM roles.

# Required Checks

- Dependency and SAST scanning before merge.
- Threat model updates for new high-risk flows.
- Authentication and authorization coverage for all protected APIs.
- Audit logging for sensitive actions and admin operations.

# Data Protection

- Encrypt data in transit and at rest.
- Mask PII in logs, traces, and test artifacts.
